✅ CSS Types
What is the difference between Internal, Inline, and External CSS? Give one advantage of each.
1)internal css: we align it within the html file below the title tag as <style> </style>. its helpful
                when we want to add css into 1 single file with html
  
2)inline css: we align the as <h1 style="color:red;">hello</h1>. its helps when we want an single 
              element to give some specific decoration

3)External css: we make diffrent file of css then we attach itwith html using <link href="style.css"           rel="stylesheet" type="text/css"/>. its can be helpful if the css is so large then we should use this method.

Write an example of each CSS type (Internal, Inline, and External) using an <h1> tag.
internal css: <h1>Hello World!</h1>   
            <style> 
                h1 {
                    color:red;
                }    
            </style> 

inline css: <h1 style="color:red;">Hello World!</h1>   

external css: <h1>Hello World!</h1>
              <link href="style.css" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css"/>

